WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.110
Good morning Hank.

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:02.110
It's Tuesday.

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:03.429
So yesterday some friends and I went to the
Indianapolis Motor Speedway, and I got to

00:00:03.429 --> 00:00:07.480
drive around the track with race car driver
Sarah Fisher at 180 miles per hour and experience

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:10.719
profound fear-joy, which would be a good name
for a band.

00:00:10.719 --> 00:00:13.610
But for now the relevant thing is while I
was going around the track I felt like Sarah

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:16.219
Fisher was driving the Batmobile and I was
Robin.

00:00:16.219 --> 00:00:20.410
And that reminded me that while I'm a big
Sarah Fisher fan, I kind of hate Batman.

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:23.820
Like Hank, if I were a billionaire, the first
thing I would do would be to pledge 90% of

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:24.820
my money to charity.

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:27.510
Then I would build my own race track that
Sarah Fisher could drive me around, then I

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:30.200
would give AFC Wimbledon a bunch of money
so they could build a new stadium.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:33.570
Then I'd build a huge house with lots of secret
rooms that you can only access by touching

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:38.760
certain books on a fake bookshelf, and then
I would still be SUPER rich because a billion

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.370
dollars is a lot of money...

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:41.720
but I am getting slightly off topic here.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:44.570
The point being, Hank, I don't think I'd be
a particularly good or generous billionaire,

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:49.240
but one thing I wouldn't do is spend a gajillion
dollars developing a Batmobile that only I

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:50.720
am allowed to drive.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:55.390
I mean look Hank, Spiderman go bit by a radioactive
spider; he has to be Spiderman; he doesn't

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:59.559
have a choice; he can't stop shooting webs
so you might as well use that skill to aid

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:00.559
the police.

00:01:00.559 --> 00:01:04.150
Similarly, Sailor Moon didn't choose to be
an alien princess from Silver Millennium,

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:08.850
but Batman is just a rich guy with an affinity
for bats who's playing out his insane fantasy

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:12.100
of single handedly ridding Gotham of crime;
how is that heroic?

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:16.380
Now I know what you're saying Hank- Iron Man-
and fair enough, Tony Stark is a billionaire

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:18.130
who could use his wealth a little bit better.

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:22.230
And that's a story unto itself about how the
superheroes elevated by each generation say

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:23.400
a lot about that generation.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:26.990
But at least Iron Man has that weird nuclear
bomb heart thing built with the help of the

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:29.080
token good, and therefore doomed Arab guy.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:31.760
And then he's like "Aw I should use my nuclear
heart for good."

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:33.060
It's not much but it's something.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:35.590
Meanwhile can you really argue that Batman
is good for Gotham?

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:38.640
I mean in the Batman universe crime is caused
by:

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:39.640
1.

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:40.740
Evil people who just wanna see the world burn
and

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:41.740
2.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:46.000
Stupid people who follow the evil but charismatic
cat person/joker/penguin.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.470
God, the villains in Batman are terrible.

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:53.130
Also, slightly off topic but I would argue
that Catwoman despite her jewelry thieving

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:56.860
etc. is by almost any measure much more heroic
than Batman.

00:01:56.860 --> 00:02:01.880
But anyway, crime is not actually caused by
evil; it's caused by systemic disenfranchisement

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:05.729
and poverty and lack of access to job opportunities
and education.

00:02:05.729 --> 00:02:10.899
And yet Batman continues on, not funding police
departments or schools or building low income

00:02:10.899 --> 00:02:15.200
housing, but tearing up the infrastructure
of the city he claims to love while fighting

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:20.530
villains who are only powerful because that
city is already so blighted and dysfunctional.

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:24.290
I'm sorry I'm losing my temper, but does Batman
understand how difficult it is for an under-funded

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:26.780
city like Gotham to replace roads and bridges?

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:30.200
Anyway Hank, it seems to me that one of the
more realistic facets of the Batman saga is

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:35.310
that Gotham never gets better for long after
Batman's villain-destroying exploits.

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:39.610
Batman saves Gotham over and over and over
again, but he never actually improves it.

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:43.400
Also, why does no one ever call Batman out
for devoting all of his resources to fighting

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:44.489
crime in Gotham?

00:02:44.489 --> 00:02:48.690
When he could also be fighting, I don't know,
global poverty or habitat destruction or climate

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:49.690
change.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:52.459
Now Hank I'm not saying that cleaning up the
streets of Gotham isn't a worthy goal for

00:02:52.459 --> 00:02:54.800
a billionaire, but to reiterate, he's bad
at it.

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:58.650
I will say this, Hank, Batman has inspired
some great graphic novels and some very good

00:02:58.650 --> 00:02:59.650
movies.

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:02.350
All of which go to extraordinary lengths to
make it seem like bad things just keep happening

00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:05.560
to Batman, so he has to develop a massive
arsenal that he keeps in a Batcave.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:09.129
But Hank, the question at the core of the
Batman story still bothers me.

00:03:09.129 --> 00:03:13.129
Why do we celebrate the vigilantic ambitions
of individual billionaires?

00:03:13.129 --> 00:03:18.910
Surely we understand that the real work among
humans is done not in isolation but in collaboration?

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:21.170
We do understand that, right?

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:25.050
And no I am not just saying all of this because
my hair looks more and more like Wolverine's

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:26.090
by the day.

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:27.590
Hank, I will see you on Friday.

